# Quiz Component for the Crash Course

## Finish line

NOT YET PINNED — the charter grilling has not happened. Joel asked first for a
trace of what exists. Research steps run first; the finish line gets pinned with
`grill-me` once the facts are in hand.

Draft conditions, to be confirmed or replaced:

- Matt can author a text quiz inline in a crash-course lesson body and it
  renders, accepts an answer, and tells the learner whether they were right.
- Matt (or his agent) has a documented API path for creating and editing quiz
  content without hand-editing app code.
- Answers persist somewhere Joel is willing to maintain, at a durability level
  both parties agreed to on purpose.
- Whoever maintains this after launch can find the quiz data, the renderer, and
  the persistence path from one entry point.

## Vocabulary

- **quiz** — a set of questions that have correct answers and grade the learner.
  Distinct from a survey, which collects opinions and has no correctness.
- **survey** — the existing AI Hero / course-builder system for collecting
  learner answers with no notion of right or wrong.
- **crash course** — the AI Hero product surface Matt named in the request;
  exact identity to be confirmed by research.
- **inline authoring** — the quiz question and its answers live in the lesson's
  MDX body, not in a separate record the author creates first. This is Matt's
  stated preference and it is in tension with Joel's data-driven position.
- **data-driven authoring** — quiz content is a content resource, fetched over
  the same API as every other resource; MDX carries only a reference.

## Notes

- Domain: AI Hero app (`~/Code/badass-courses/ai-hero`, `apps/ai-hero`) plus the
  course-builder monorepo (`~/Code/badass-courses/course-builder`, notably
  `packages/survey`, `packages/adapter-drizzle`, `packages/ui`).
- Source of the request: Matt Pocock in Slack `#cc-matt-p`, thread
  `https://eggheadio.slack.com/archives/C0211NSK3TP/p1784717959599139`
  (2026-07-24). Tagged `:shitrat:` on the root.
- What Matt asked for, verbatim in substance:
  - A `<Quiz>` component for the crash course, text-based questions only.
  - Persisted answers preferred; `localStorage` explicitly acceptable to him.
  - It must work inline in the lesson body.
  - Shape `<Quiz><QuizQuestion data={} /></Quiz>`, with the question and answer
    baked in so there is "no extra thing to author" — this makes it easy for his
    agent to generate and edit quizzes.
  - "Yep as long as I've got an API for it I'm OK."
- What Joel said in the thread: the survey system already is quizzes; an MDX
  component may need wiring but "the hard bits are done/baked in"; it is data
  driven, content resources, over the same API.
- Open tension to grill: Matt wants content inline in MDX, Joel wants content
  resources over the API. Matt's last message suggests an API satisfies him, but
  that has not been confirmed against his authoring loop.
- Skills to consult: `grill-me`, `herdr-orchestration`, `prototype`.
- Execution authorization: NOT granted. Sessions produce decisions until Joel
  says otherwise.

## Decision ledger

- [Trace the course-builder survey primitives](./trace-coursebuilder-survey-primitives.svx)
  — `@coursebuilder/survey` is a quiz engine named "survey": machine id is
  `quizMachine`, questions carry `correct` + `answer`, and the machine grades into
  `answered.correct`/`incorrect`/`neutral`. Five gaps to a real quiz, including a
  multi-select grading bug that accepts a proper subset as fully correct.
- [Trace the AI Hero survey system end to end](./trace-ai-hero-survey-system.svx)
  — Surveys and questions are `contentResource` rows joined by
  `contentResourceResource`; answers are `QuestionResponse.fields.answer` mirrored
  to Kit. The REST API covers surveys only: **there is no question CRUD endpoint**,
  and the admin form does not expose `correct`. No supported path can author a
  graded question today.
- [Trace AI Hero MDX rendering and the crash course](./trace-ai-hero-mdx-and-crash-course.svx)
  — Lesson bodies compile through `next-mdx-remote/rsc` at request time with
  `blockJS: false`. Structured object props work (`ThemeImage urls={{...}}` ships
  today), stateful client components work, and no quiz component is registered.
  Crash-course content flows Course Video Manager → Dropbox `/course.json` →
  course-sync, whose v3 schema carries `body` strings and rejects extra properties.

## Latent

- Whether quiz answers should feed the existing subscriber/segmentation
  machinery the surveys feed, or stay inert learner-facing state.
- Whether this ships as an AI Hero-only component or a `@coursebuilder/*`
  primitive other apps inherit. AI Hero pins `@coursebuilder/survey@^1.0.5` while
  the source package is at `1.0.13` — any package-level change has to cross that
  version gap.
- How quiz content gets reviewed and kept correct as course content changes.
- Whether the accumulated dead surfaces found during the trace get cleaned up as
  part of this work or logged separately: the commented-out published-state check
  on `/survey/[slug]`, `deleteSurvey` orphaning question resources, unwritten
  `respondentKey`/`surveySessionId` columns, and the unimported analytics provider.

